## Detailed Flow Analysis with Audit Control

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant React as React Frontend
    participant Server as Express Backend (Port 5001)
    participant Pi as Raspberry Pi (Python)
    participant DB as MongoDB / SQLite

    User->>React: Click "Start Audit"
    React->>Server: POST /api/audit-sessions
    Server->>DB: Create session with status "active"
    Server-->>React: Session active confirmation

    Note over User, Pi: Scenario A: Scan occurs during active audit
    User->>Pi: Scan barcode
    Pi->>Server: POST /api/barcode (with barcode)
    Server->>DB: Check if active session exists
    Note over Server: Active session exists
    Server->>DB: Save scan to BCScan (MongoDB)
    Server->>React: Broadcast live scan via WebSocket (Port 8080)
    Server-->>Pi: 200 OK (Scan Saved)
    Pi->>DB: Write scan to local SQLite (for sync integrity)

    Note over User, Pi: Scenario B: Scan occurs when no audit is active
    User->>Pi: Scan barcode
    Pi->>Server: POST /api/barcode (with barcode)
    Server->>DB: Check if active session exists
    Note over Server: No active session exists
    Server-->>Pi: 400 Bad Request {error: "NO_ACTIVE_AUDIT"}
    Pi->>Pi: Skip writing to local SQLite database (Discard scan)
```

